# Eddymurk Crab: Flash, "This creature enters tapped if it's not your turn", "When this creature enters, tap up to two target creatures."
# On turn 1 Bot1 casts one Lightning Bolt (so the Crab costs {1} less: {4}{U}{U} = six, exactly the six blue mana of two Mox Sapphires, an Island
# and a Black Lotus). On Bot2's turn 2, after Bot2 has cast two Llanowar Elves and an Ornithopter, Bot1 flashes the Crab in: it is not Bot1's turn, so it
# enters tapped (CR 614.1d), and its trigger taps two of the three creatures - three cannot be chosen (up to two) - leaving the third untapped.
# (The control, where it is Bot1's own turn and the Crab enters untapped, is the neighbouring scenario.)

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Black Lotus
Eddymurk Crab
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Llanowar Elves
Llanowar Elves
Ornithopter
Island
Island
Forest x13

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
